Tuesday Update
*&nbsp; Trade Alert: FUBO calls in gear; buy WDAY calls* Stocks chop around=
 again as investors await earnings reports and Fed decisionStock indexes ar=
e poised to continue gaining ground as investors look to buy dips in the in=
dex and drive up the measure, according to Janney Montgomery Scott.In a not=
e, technical strategist and associate director of research Dan Wantrobski s=
aid drops in the index have proven to be buying triggers for bullish invest=
ors. And there could be further room to run in the years ahead, he added."I=
t would appear that liquidity truly remains king these days, and we do beli=
eve that based on this ongoing phenomenon (which is unprecedented), the S&a=
mp;P 500 should be able to hit that 4,000 mark at some point in 2021," Want=
robski said in a note on Tuesday.The benchmark S&amp;P 500 was down about 0=
.2% in early afternoon trading to just below 3,850. The index hit a record =
high of 3,855.36 on Monday and is up about 14% over the past three months, =
buoyed in part by hopes that vaccines against COVID-19 will speed up an end=
 to the pandemic.Still, Janney's modelling doesn't show 2021 as the peak cy=
cle of the so-called current bull market, Wantrobski said. In the years ahe=
ad, the S&amp;P 500 target is in the 4,500 to 5,000 zone, he added. If the =
buy-the-dip pattern breaks and a bigger correction takes place before the m=
easure hits 4,000, Wantrobski said "we would still encourage investors to m=
aintain their equity exposure and deploy sideline cash opportunistically."H=
eavier selling could be triggered by risks including earnings results, mone=
tary and fiscal policy, vaccine implications and trends in interest rates, =
he said. "Any significant developments along these lines could disrupt the =
buy-the-dip pattern and trigger heavier selling, which quickly breaks 3,800=
 SPX and targets the 3,750 range as an important level in our opinion.=E2=
=80=9DPortfolio: Our new FUBO calls are trading higher; adjust stop. AAPL o=
rder did not fill. We have one new idea today.&nbsp;*CURRENT RECOMMENDATION=
SfuboTV Inc. (FUBO) February $40 calls-- Symbol: FUBO210219C00040000-- Orde=
r filled at $7.10 on Monday Jan. 25. -- Now trading at $7.60.-- Set up to s=
